-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 F = 2.0
' X ^ 0 gives 1 and X ^ 1 gives X; a constant 0 or 1 exponent is reduced by
' the compiler and warned about. The base is a variable so it reaches codegen.
' Both Integer (0%) and Single (0) constant exponents are covered.
20 A = F ^ 0%
30 A = F ^ 1%
40 A = F ^ 0
50 A = F ^ 1.0
' X ^ 2 is a real power, no warning
60 A = F ^ 2%
----------------------------------------------------------------------
